Injection points for the port's tests, at five of Apache Cloudberry's
faults inside PostgreSQL's own replication code, which its FTS tests in
isolation2 hold or count (src/test/isolation2/sql/segwalrep), and one at
the start of a simple query, which dtx_recovery_wait_lsn there fails the
coordinator at:

  wal-sender-loop          walsender.c, WalSndLoop()        wal_sender_loop
  wal-sender-after-send    walsender.c, WalSndLoop()        wal_sender_after_caughtup_within_range
  walrecv-skip-flush       walreceiver.c, XLogWalRcvFlush() walrecv_skip_flush
  sync-rep-query-die       syncrep.c, SyncRepWaitForLSN()   sync_rep_query_die
  sync-rep-query-cancel    syncrep.c, SyncRepWaitForLSN()   sync_rep_query_cancel
  exec-simple-query-start  postgres.c, exec_simple_query()  exec_simple_query_start

And three more of its faults, under their own names, which the tests of
greenplum_schedule set: an autovacuum worker's before it vacuums a
database, and the update of the database's row that vacuuming it ends
with (the autovacuum tests), each giving the fault's callback the
database's name, as Cloudberry's call does; and a count of rows made
almost 2^32 where a "skip" asks, in the executor's run and a SELECT's
count of its rows, which SPI's check of its count then passes over, as
Cloudberry's does (the processed64bit tests):

  auto_vac_worker_before_do_autovacuum  autovacuum.c, AutoVacWorkerMain()
  vacuum_update_dat_frozen_xid          vacuum.c, vac_update_datfrozenxid()
  executor_run_high_processed           execMain.c, standard_ExecutorRun()
                                        and ExecutePlan(); spi.c, _SPI_pquery()

gp_core's fault injector attaches a fault of Cloudberry's name to the point
(gp_fault.c); walrecv-skip-flush is given a bool its callback sets to skip
the flush.  They serve tests alone, so they are not in the core series:
Dockerfile.pg applies this to the tree of either ref, vanilla or patched,
so that the two images still differ only in the ref.  Dormant, as any
point is: without injection points the macro is empty, and with them a
point nothing attached to runs no callback.


